  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit; the priority is to establish a performance baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the design space: it uses a linear, parameter-free RNA encoder (PCA), a single profile (no aggregation), and no image modality. This gives a clean 'floor' reference for validation accuracy and F1 against which every other design decision (multiprofile aggregation, learned RNA encoders, image modality, multimodal fusion) can be measured. Establishing this baseline first is the most information-dense use of the first experiment because it anchors all subsequent comparisons and reveals how much headroom each design axis has to improve upon."
